  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner who became famous for completing marathons in a bionic suit after being paralysed in a 2007 horse riding accident, has died following an accident in Jordan on August 22. Lomas, who raised nearly £1 million for charity, was paralysed from the chest down when her horse threw her at the Osberton Horse Trials, breaking her neck, back, and ribs. She gained national attention for completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days wearing a bionic suit and was honored by lighting the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square. In 2016, she completed the Great North Run in five days while pregnant, again using her bionic suit. Her family has asked for privacy as they grieve."
}
```

